msgid "Consolidate for a target"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Check what a viewer will find, model by model, before you hand the study"
" on.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A study published on Heriverse, opened on a phone, or loaded in a "
"realtime engine does not show the heavy master of each model: it loads a "
"version made for that use. ``File ▸ Export ▸ Consolidate for…`` opens the"
" list of the study's assets read for one *target*, so that you can see, "
"before handing the study on, which assets have a version for it, how "
"heavy the whole scene will be, and what is still to do. Nothing is "
"written while you read: the files and the graph change only when an "
"action of the queue runs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Before you start"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Open the study. Its models and their versions are read from the graph and"
" measured from their files, so the files should be on this computer (see "
":doc:`/how-to/files/find-missing-files`)."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The list is computed by the bridge. If the bridge is too old, the view "
"says which level it needs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Open the list for a target"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Choose ``File ▸ Export ▸ Consolidate for…``. EMStudio switches to the "
"**Archive** workspace and puts the **Files** window in its **Assets** "
"mode. The first time, a bar shows the reading: the graph, the resources, "
"the measuring of the files, the textures."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the menu at the top left, choose the **Target**: **mobile webXR**, "
"**Heriverse / web**, **desktop realtime** or **archive**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To set two or more targets side by side, tick **Compare** and switch on "
"the other targets with the buttons that appear beside it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Refresh** asks the list again, measuring anew the files that have "
"changed."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the card of the target"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The Files window in the mode Assets after File ▸ Export ▸ Consolidate "
"for…: the card of the target Heriverse / web, incomplete, with its bars "
"for triangles, download and GPU memory, and the list of the assets "
"grouped by container."
msgstr ""

msgid "Each target switched on has a card at the top of the view. It gives:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"a word for the whole scene: **inside the band**, **outside the band**, or"
" **incomplete** while some assets still have no version for this target, "
"in which case the numbers estimate what a viewer would load;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"how many assets are covered, for example **2 / 98 covered**, and, after "
"an arrow, how many will be covered when the queue has run;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"three bars, **Triangles**, **Download MB** and **GPU MB**, against the "
"band of the target. The light bar is today, the dark bar is after the "
"queue;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the limits for one object, for example the triangles and the texture size"
" a single model may have. For **archive** there is no ceiling: what "
"counts is the master, stamped and present."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Under these figures, the card says what the version of the target is made"
" of (see :doc:`versions-for-each-use`)."
msgstr ""

msgid "Read the assets"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each row is an asset, with the columns **Asset / version / texture**, "
"**Level**, **Triangles**, **Disk MB**, **GPU MB**, **Max texture**, "
"**Tex** and **Stamp**, then one column per target, **state / proposal**. "
"A click on a column header sorts the rows by it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The state of each target is **ok**, **to do**, **missing** or **n/a**. "
"Where something is to do, the cell shows the proposal: the tool, the "
"triangles and the texture size. A value outside the band is highlighted."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Narrow the list with **Search assets…**, with the filter **All**, **Only "
"to do** or **Only over the band**, and with the grouping: by container "
"(the default), branch, epoch, family of name or state, or **No groups**."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click ▸ to open an asset on its versions and their textures; **open all**"
" opens every asset. **Textures** lists every texture of the study once, "
"with its size, its weight and where it is used."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A click on a row lights it and shows its detail in the panel on the "
"right, which **Show the row's panel (N)** opens and closes."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Some rows are read together. Copies of the same shape, with the same "
"geometry and textures, are gathered under one row **repeated shape ×** "
"followed by the number of copies, with one proposal: one reduced mesh and"
" as many instances. Meshes already covered by a tileset say **by the "
"tileset of** followed by its name, and stay out of the count. A version "
"in the cloud, not yet downloaded, is counted with the graph's estimate; "
"**⤓ Download and measure** fetches it, after saying how much it weighs."
msgstr ""

msgid "Do what is to do"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tick the rows to treat, or the box at the top of the list for all the "
"rows shown. A group has a box of its own."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Click **Apply and queue**. The proposal of each row, for the targets "
"switched on, goes into the queue in one step. You can first change the "
"proposal of a row in its cell."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"If every object fits its band but the scene does not, the window **The "
"scene is still over its band** proposes a second round: it lists the rows"
" to shrink further, repeated shapes first, then the heaviest objects, "
"with the triangles of the scene before and after. Choose **Shrink these "
"too**, **Only the proposal**, or cancel."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The **Queue** runs each action in turn. **Run** starts the actions as "
"their turn comes; **Pause** lets them pile up. The head of the queue says"
" when it should end, for example **ends around 22:30**, from the "
"durations measured on this computer."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An action that cannot start says why on its row, with the gesture that "
"solves it: a tool to install, a source to stamp first, Blender to find. "
"The others go on."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The queue also has a view of its own: choose **Queue** in the mode menu "
"of the **Files** window, or click **Open the Queue**. It shows one row "
"per job, with its asset, target, tool, state, progress, time and outcome,"
" and filters for **running**, **waiting**, **failed** and **done**."
msgstr ""

msgid "What you get"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Each action of the queue writes a version of a model, stamped as derived "
"from its master, and registers it in the graph as a version of its asset."
" The card of the target then counts it: when every asset is covered and "
"the bars stay inside the band, the study is ready for that target."
msgstr ""

msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`versions-for-each-use`, for the versions themselves and how to "
"manage them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`storage`, to put the files in the room or in the bucket where the "
"target reads them."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/space/load-models-and-tilesets`, for the version the 3D "
"scene loads on this machine."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
":doc:`/how-to/extensions/compose-a-blend`, for a working ``.blend`` "
"composed from the graph, the other command beside **Consolidate for…**."
msgstr ""

